python .\experiments\reproduce_locked_candidate_98.py

## Step 3B — Restore `docs/methodology.md`

This command rewrites the methodology file with just the methodology content, removing the accidental duplicate document:

```powershell
@'
# Research methodology (working draft)

## Research question

Can evidence-aware root-cause ranking remain useful and appropriately
cautious when telemetry is incomplete or noisy, while making its
reasoning inspectable by a developer?

## Scope

TraceWise AI is a local research prototype for microservice incident
investigation. Its intended workflow ingests timestamped event records,
extracts signals, ranks candidate explanations, links hypotheses to
observed evidence, and presents counter-evidence and diagnostic checks.

The repository contains two distinct components:

1. A developer-facing prototype with illustrative synthetic incident records.
2. A separate experimental evaluation pipeline for labelled RCAEval cases.

The benchmark evaluator is not evidence that the UI's scenario controls
run the benchmark pipeline.

## Current implementation

The UI/API prototype uses a deterministic, interpretable heuristic
baseline. Its documented signal families include database or pool
pressure, timeouts or latency, and retries. A modest temporal boost is
used when a pool signal precedes a timeout.

The separate benchmark candidate calculates metric-level scores from
pre-fault and post-fault medians, scales changes using robust dispersion
with a relative scale floor, and aggregates available metric scores into
service-level rankings.

These methods produce relative scores. They are not calibrated
probabilities, and neither temporal order nor a high ranking proves
causation.

## Benchmark protocol

The frozen candidate is V2 all-metric mean:

- Robust scale: 1.4826 × median absolute deviation
- Effective scale: maximum of robust scale, 1% of the absolute pre-fault
  median, and 1e-9
- Metric score: absolute post/pre median change divided by effective scale
- Service aggregation: arithmetic mean of available metric scores
- Ranking: competition ranking, with ties sharing the same rank
- Pre-fault window: injection time −300 to −60 seconds, inclusive
- Post-fault window: injection time +60 to +300 seconds, inclusive

The evaluation uses 98 exploratory RCAEval cases. Two cases were
excluded because their recorded injection timestamps were incompatible
with available telemetry. The source timestamps have not been silently
changed. Details are recorded in
`experiments/results/excluded_case_timestamp_audit.md`.

## Exploratory results

| Version | Hit@1 | Hit@3 | MRR | Mean correct-service rank |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| V1 | 58.16% | 70.41% | 0.686152 | 2.8061 |
| V2, 1% scale floor | 64.29% | 78.57% | 0.737366 | 2.4592 |

V2 reports better ranking metrics on this 98-case exploratory evaluation.
Because the set has informed development, this is not independent
validation and does not establish generalization to unseen datasets.

The reproduction script generated matching case-result, service-ranking,
metric-evidence, and summary outputs from the current implementation and
inputs. This supports reproducibility of the saved outputs, not external
validity.

## Proposed further evaluation

- Review relevant literature and compare with suitable published baselines.
- Resolve excluded cases only with authoritative metadata or replacement data.
- Establish an independent validation set or defensible untouched split.
- Inject controlled missing telemetry and noise with fixed random seeds.
- Report Hit@1, Hit@3, mean reciprocal rank, and appropriate uncertainty.
- Run ablations for temporal features, service relationships, and evidence filtering.
- If abstention is implemented, report coverage alongside selective risk.
- Assess calibration only where the output and experimental design support it.

## Validity and safety limitations

A timestamp order is not proof of causation. Heuristic ranking scores
are not probabilities. Synthetic incidents are for UI development only.
The 98-case evaluation is exploratory, and independent validation is not
currently available. Claims must be restricted to documented experiments.

Do not use this prototype to trigger automated production remediation.
